To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$ and $\blueD{\text{multiply it by } 2} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{9}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD {y} &=\greenD{9} \blueD{\times 2} \\\\
\maroonD {y}&=\maroonD{18}
\end{align}$

To find the value of $\greenD{x}$, divide both sides of the equation by $2$:

$\begin{align}
\blueD{\dfrac{\maroonD{10}}{2}}&=\blueD{\dfrac{\blueD{2}\greenD{x}}{2}} \\\\
\greenD{5} &= \greenD{x}
\end{align}$
